> rl(x: u16, n: u16 in 1..15) = (x << n) | (x >> (16 - n))
> rr(x: u16, n: u16 in 1..15) = (x >> n) | (x << (16 - n))
> equiv rl rr
rl and rr differ at 916896 points, e.g. x=1, n=1: 2 vs 32768
> rl2(x: u16, n: u16 in 1..15) = (x >> (16 - n)) | (x << n)
> equiv rl rl2
rl and rl2 are equal on the domain of rl (exhaustive)
> rng(x: u16, n: u16 in 1..15) = (x << n) & 0xffff
> range rng
range of rng -> u16:
  0..65534   (32768 distinct values)
  fits in u16
  over all 983040 points of the domain
> mask8(x: u8) = x & 0x0f
> range mask8
range of mask8 -> u8:
  0..15   (16 distinct values)
  values: 0..15
  fits in u4
  over all 256 points of the domain
> domain mask8
domain of mask8:
  x: u8, 0..255
  defined at 256 of 256 points
  no conditions: total on its parameter types
  over all 256 points of the domain
